ferrometer (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Logs auto-format for journald when stderr is hooked to it: timestamps
    dropped (journald has its own), ANSI colors dropped, syslog `<N>`
    priority prefix per line so journald assigns the right PRIORITY field.
    Otherwise the human-friendly format is unchanged.
  * Unix collector emits `node_memory_Dirty_bytes`.

 -- Roman Kivalin <roman@shl.dev>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ferrometer (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial release.
  * Collectors: Unix system metrics (CPU + frequency/governor/throttle,
    memory, disk incl. discards/flushes, filesystem, network, load average,
    uname); Prometheus scraper for any text-exposition /metrics endpoint.
  * Log shipping: systemd journal source with persisted cursor, Loki sink
    speaking the native protobuf + snappy push API. Per-shipper exponential
    backoff. journald itself is the durable buffer during a sink outage.
  * Forwarders: OTLP HTTP push with gzip compression, in-memory ring buffer,
    exponential backoff, configurable OTLP Resource attributes.
  * Auth: basic / bearer / arbitrary Authorization header on every HTTP
    client. Secrets via env vars, files, or systemd encrypted credentials.
  * mTLS with optional custom CA bundle on every HTTP client.
  * TOML configuration with ${instance.name} / ${version} / ${env:VAR}
    placeholder expansion and load-time validation.
  * Hardened systemd service unit running under a transient DynamicUser
    inside a locked-down sandbox.

 -- Roman Kivalin <roman@shl.dev>  Sat, 25 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
